Cell[TextData[{
 "and similar diagrams with the photon (generate u d~ > ve e+ d d~ QED=4 \
QCD=0). In the case of QED we have more diagrams, but don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t \
worry, Furry theorem kills all the QiQj contributions. Only Qi^2 terms will \
survive, which are the diagrams 2 and diagram 3 with a photon replacing \
gluons. For this reason, q\[CloseCurlyQuote]\[CloseCurlyQuote] cannot be any \
kind of quark! ",
 StyleBox["q\[CloseCurlyQuote]\[CloseCurlyQuote] must be q\[CloseCurlyQuote], \
q, q\[CloseCurlyQuote]~ or q~",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". BUT q\[CloseCurlyQuote] has a different triple-collinear structure!"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9452454408910713`*^9, {3.945245535022139*^9, 3.945245638058909*^9}, {
   3.966075751789444*^9, 3.966075755901279*^9}, {3.966075892067272*^9, 
   3.9660760154278917`*^9}, {3.966611405357319*^9, 3.9666116412266207`*^9}, {
